I&#x27;m not sure I understand you, or you understand me. I&#x27;m saying this is okay:<p><pre><code>  type Order struct {
   Type        OrderType
   CommonAttr1 int
   CommonAttr2 string
  }

  type OrderTypeA struct {
   Order
   TypeAAttr1 int
   TypeAAttr2 string
  }

  type OrderTypeB struct {
   Order
   TypeBAttr1 int
   TypeBAttr2 string
  }
</code></pre>
And yes you should convert to OrderTypeA or OrderTypeB at the first opportunity in domain code, and only convert from them at the latest opportunity.<p>You seem to be under the impression that I&#x27;m advocating for something like<p><pre><code>  type OrderUnion struct {
   CommonAttr1 int
   CommonAttr2 string
   TypeAAttrs
   TypeBAttrs
  }
</code></pre>
That&#x27;s what I consider going crazy.

Struct embedding is sugar for<p><pre><code>   type Foo struct {
      MyType MyType
   }

   myFoo.MyType.url
</code></pre>
So it would resolve myFoo.MyType1.url over myFoo.MyType2.NestedType.url
